{# The skeleton of a page of the account (architecture §5.2): a page somebody reads and comes back to,
   holding a list, a table, a heading and the way to the next one.

   Three parts. A column on the side carries the pages of the account, under the headings this application
   arranges them under (App\Account\AccountNavigation), so that every one of them is one click away from
   every other and the page being read says so. A bar above carries what is true of the whole plane: the
   language, the theme, and who the browser is signed in as with the way out under their name. What is left
   is the page, which opens the same way whatever it holds: where the reader is, the title, the action the
   page offers, then what the page says. It takes the width the screen has and not the width of a box, a
   table of sessions, of consents or of acts being read across; a paragraph is held to the width of a
   column of text by the stylesheet and not by the page.

   On a screen too narrow for the column beside the page, the column slides over the page and a veil closes
   it again. That is a checkbox and a stylesheet, never a script: the pages of this plane carry none, and a
   browser that runs nothing opens and closes this one with the keyboard. #}
{% extends 'layout/document.html.twig' %}

{% block body %}
    {% set route = app.request.attributes.get('_route') ?? '' %}
    {% set groups = account_navigation(user ?? null) %}
    {# the page of the navigation this one hangs from, when it is a page under one of them: the enrolment
       of a second factor is read under the second factor, and the breadcrumb says both #}
    {% set parent = groups|reduce((pages, group) => pages|merge(group.pages), [])|filter(page => route starts with page.route ~ '_')|first %}
    <div class="flex min-h-dvh">
        <input type="checkbox" id="layout-pages-switch" aria-label="{{ 'navigation.show_pages'|trans([], 'beffroi') }}">
        <aside id="layout-sidebar">
            <div id="layout-sidebar-brand">
                {% if tenant is not null and tenant.logoUri is not null %}
                    {% include '@Beffroi/_brand.html.twig' %}
                {% else %}
                    <p class="truncate text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight">{{ tenant is not null ? tenant.name : 'account.title'|trans([], 'beffroi') }}</p>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
            {# The pages of the account under their headings, the home above every heading. A group names
               the list it heads, so that a reader who listens to the page is told which heading a link is
               under and not only that there are ten of them; the icon is drawn and never read aloud. #}
            <nav id="layout-sidebar-pages" aria-label="{{ 'navigation.pages'|trans([], 'beffroi') }}">
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <a href="{{ path('beffroi_interaction_account') }}"{% if route == 'beffroi_interaction_account' %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
                            {%- include 'layout/icon/house.html.twig' -%}
                            {{- 'account.title'|trans([], 'beffroi') -}}
                        </a>
                    </li>
                </ul>
                {% for group in groups %}
                    {% set heading = group.title is not null ? group.title|trans([], 'beffroi') : null %}
                    <div data-group>
                        {% if heading is not null %}<p data-group-title aria-hidden="true">{{ heading }}</p>{% endif %}
                        <ul{% if heading is not null %} aria-label="{{ heading }}"{% endif %}>
                            {% for page in group.pages %}
                                <li>
                                    <a href="{{ path(page.route) }}"{% if route == page.route or route starts with page.route ~ '_' %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
                                        {%- if page.icon is not null %}{% include 'layout/icon/' ~ page.icon ~ '.html.twig' ignore missing %}{% endif -%}
                                        <span>{{ page.title|trans([], 'beffroi') }}</span>
                                        {%- if page.count is not null %}<span data-count="{{ page.count }}">{{ page.count }}</span>{% endif -%}
                                    </a>
                                </li>
                            {% endfor %}
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                {% endfor %}
            </nav>
        </aside>
        <label for="layout-pages-switch" id="layout-sidebar-veil" aria-hidden="true"></label>
        <div class="flex min-h-dvh min-w-0 grow flex-col">
            <header id="layout-topbar">
                <label for="layout-pages-switch" id="layout-pages-button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-square btn-sm" aria-hidden="true">
                    {% include 'layout/icon/menu.html.twig' with {size: 'size-5'} %}
                </label>
                {# where the column of pages is not shown, the bar says whose provider this is #}
                <a href="{{ path('beffroi_interaction_account') }}" id="layout-topbar-home" class="lg:hidden">
                    {{- tenant is not null ? tenant.name : 'account.title'|trans([], 'beffroi') -}}
                </a>
                <div class="ms-auto flex items-center gap-2">
                    {% include 'layout/_controls.html.twig' %}
                    {# Who the browser is signed in as is the button, and what they can do about it is what
                       opens under it: the name is read once, where the way out is, every page of this
                       plane being a page of that person. A page served to a browser that holds no session
                       says so in its own words and has nobody to name. #}
                    {% if user is defined %}
                        {% embed 'layout/_control.html.twig' with {control: 'user', label: 'account.title'|trans([], 'beffroi')} %}
                            {% block trigger %}
                                {%- include 'layout/icon/user.html.twig' -%}
                                <span class="max-sm:hidden">{{ user.username }}</span>
                                {%- include 'layout/icon/chevron.html.twig' with {size: 'size-3.5'} -%}
                            {% endblock %}
                            {% block panel %}
                                <ul class="menu">
                                    <li>
                                        <a href="{{ path('beffroi_interaction_account_profile') }}">
                                            {%- include 'layout/icon/card.html.twig' -%}
                                            {{- 'profile.title'|trans([], 'beffroi') -}}
                                        </a>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        <a href="{{ path('beffroi_interaction_logout') }}">
                                            {%- include 'layout/icon/exit.html.twig' -%}
                                            {{- 'account.sign_out'|trans([], 'beffroi') -}}
                                        </a>
                                    </li>
                                </ul>
                            {% endblock %}
                        {% endembed %}
                    {% endif %}
                </div>
            </header>
            <div id="layout-content">
                <main data-page="account" class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-[84rem] flex-col gap-6">
                    {# Every page of the plane opens the same way: where the reader is, what the page is,
                       and the one action it offers, which is beside the title and not at the end of what
                       the page says. A page that offers none fills the block with nothing. #}
                    <header data-page-header>
                        <nav aria-label="{{ 'navigation.where_you_are'|trans([], 'beffroi') }}">
                            <ol>
                                <li>
                                    {%- if route == 'beffroi_interaction_account' -%}
                                        <span aria-current="page">{{ 'account.title'|trans([], 'beffroi') }}</span>
                                    {%- else -%}
                                        <a href="{{ path('beffroi_interaction_account') }}">{{ 'account.title'|trans([], 'beffroi') }}</a>
                                    {%- endif -%}
                                </li>
                                {% if parent %}
                                    <li><a href="{{ path(parent.route) }}">{{ parent.title|trans([], 'beffroi') }}</a></li>
                                {% endif %}
                                {% if route != 'beffroi_interaction_account' %}
                                    <li><span aria-current="page">{{ block('title') }}</span></li>
                                {% endif %}
                            </ol>
                        </nav>
                        <div data-heading-row>
                            <h1>{% block heading %}{{ block('title') }}{% endblock %}</h1>
                            {# What the page offers is one thing at the end of the line, whether the page
                               writes one element there or three: the block is wrapped here so that a page
                               that answers with a button and a word does not spread them apart. #}
                            <div data-action>{% block action %}{% endblock %}</div>
                        </div>
                    </header>
                    {% block content %}{% endblock %}
                </main>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
